# Where a target's hotspot list comes from, named in targets[].site.hotspot_source.
# The same four names are registered in HOTSPOT_SOURCES in
# the adapter image, which resolves them. The adapters ship to a container that
# does not run the executor, so the tuple lives in both places.
#
#   explicit           targets[].site.hotspot_residues carries the list
#   site-fallback      no separate hotspot list was supplied, so the metric
#                      deliberately reuses reference_contact_residues
#   designed_complex   measured on the designed complex the row is scored
#                      against, at targets[].site.contact_cutoff_angstrom
#   published_epitope  read out of the released design_summary.csv named by
#                      targets[].site.published_epitope_table
#
# Only `explicit` states an epitope chosen before design. The other two measure
# where a finished design landed. `epitope_residues` in the released table is
# retrospective, and PROVENANCE.md line 25 records that most arms chose hotspots
# autonomously with the specification column blank, so for most released designs
